# LOOP's second page (ENV there): each layer's PAN (its place, over VOX's), DRIFT (how far it sways round
# it, on the tide), TONE (its filter, darker .. brighter) and SWELL (its envelope, plucked .. slow). They are
# heard on its notes at once, the drift moves its place as the tide goes, and all of it is saved with the
# loop. ENV again: the first page. (The note recorded is held as the loop closes, the hand's and the loop's
# the same note: the key let go does not end the loop's.)
wait 1000
tap REC
key w2 down
wait 2600
tap REC
wait 100
key w2 up
expect looper 2
tap SEL
wait 100
expect view 8
expect lpage 0
tap ENV
wait 100
expect lpage 1
expect view 8
turn K1 -20
wait 300
expect lay14 24
expect vpan 24
turn K3 12
wait 300
expect lay16 88
expect vtone >200
expect vtone <240
turn K4 -10
wait 100
expect lay17 44
shot loop_place.png
turn K2 40
wait 100
expect lay15 80
expect vpan <99
wait 9000
expect vpan <99
tap ENV
wait 100
expect lpage 0
tap SAVE
wait 500
reboot
wait 3000
expect lay14 24
expect lay15 80
expect lay16 88
expect lay17 44
tap SEL
tap ENV
turn K1 20
turn K2 -40
turn K3 -12
turn K4 10
wait 300
expect lay14 64
expect lay15 0
expect vpan 64
expect vtone 100
expect clips 0
